<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49230" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trītūra</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				rubbing</i>, <i>wearing off</i>, <i>chafing.</i> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">muli pectora copulae sparteae triturā
					continuā exulcerati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p. 222, 39</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>a threshing</i>, of grain, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 21</span></i>
			Müll.; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 1, 190</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 2, 19,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 6,
			23</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
